Read LoadState together with UnitFileState in the same call:
- not-found means the producer isn't installed: inactive, "producer not installed", neither healthy nor a problem;
- enabled with stale readings is a problem;
- disabled is inactive with detail;
- any other or failed read is unreadable.

This follows Bryan's 22:07 rule that unplugging must not cause persistent failures, and stays interim until pi-config#31 moves it into config. Test all three cases.
